{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1186571-where-do-performers-and-artists-fit-in-scion-trinity","id":1186571,"title":"Where do Performers and Artists fit in Scion/Trinity?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-16T00:51:52-08:00","id":1186571,"title":"Where do Performers and Artists fit in Scion/Trinity?","content":"After looking through the rough drafts available for both Scion and Trinity, I noticed skills like Art, Performance and Expression are no longer available... which begs the question &quot;What skill(s) now cover these areas?&quot;<br /> <br /> Some skills are obvious... Subterfuge would cover the slight of hand and escape tricks that a Stage Magician would employ... but not the showmanship they also employ to wow the crowds. However, things like singing or acting don't seem to be covered as easily by any single skill available. Another problem is for artists like painters or sculptors and similar professionals that many Gods are seen as Patrons to. Where do their skill sets fit within the skills available?<br /> <br /> I have some character ideas I would like to build for these games... but not sure how to build them (which skills to take) with what's available in these settings. Any advice as to how to go about creating performers/artists would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T03:47:42-08:00","id":1186607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1186571-where-do-performers-and-artists-fit-in-scion-trinity#post1186571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After looking through the rough drafts available for both Scion and Trinity, I noticed skills like Art, Performance and Expression are no longer available... which begs the question &amp;quot;What skill(s) now cover these areas?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Some skills are obvious... Subterfuge would cover the slight of hand and escape tricks that a Stage Magician would employ... but not the showmanship they also employ to wow the crowds. However, things like singing or acting don't seem to be covered as easily by any single skill available. Another problem is for artists like painters or sculptors and similar professionals that many Gods are seen as Patrons to. Where do their skill sets fit within the skills available?<br /> <br /> I have some character ideas I would like to build for these games... but not sure how to build them (which skills to take) with what's available in these settings. Any advice as to how to go about creating performers/artists would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use another related Skill and invoke your Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T06:16:23-08:00","id":1186627,"title":"","content":"So I imagine Culture would get a fair bit of mileage for simple expression. And if you are trying to invoke a particular emotion or reaction, probably Empathy or Persuasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T06:24:32-08:00","id":1186633,"title":"","content":"You might need to make up a skill Art(type). I find both the lack of arts skills and godly powers linked to art, comunication, and language, bad signs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T06:33:15-08:00","id":1186636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1186571-where-do-performers-and-artists-fit-in-scion-trinity?p=1186633#post1186633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might need to make up a skill Art(type). I find both the lack of arts skills and godly powers linked to art, comunication, and language, bad signs.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an entire Purview dedicated to Artistry, so I don't think the Gods are lacking powers in that department.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T06:59:54-08:00","id":1186644,"title":"","content":"Culture was my assumption as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T07:06:15-08:00","id":1186647,"title":"","content":"Which makes Culture an incredibly, awesomely powerful skill","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T08:30:54-08:00","id":1186675,"title":"","content":"It may also depend on the work involved. Like, a painting may require Mental or Social + Culture to evoke the right reaction, but making a statue may require a Physical + Athletics, because hewing rock is exhausting work.<br /> <br /> Add in some Creator Knacks and the Artistry Boons and you're probably good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":".  Had to fight Autocorrect 02-16-2018, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T09:50:02-08:00","id":1186702,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I definitely like the more abstract approach taken to skills, with each being fairly broad, and in combination with Specialties, the different arenas, and your paths, how you get to different end goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T14:08:35-08:00","id":1186814,"title":"","content":"Culture does seem to fit most of the requirements for many Artist types... with some Empathy and Persuasion to help as well. Leadership could help for public speaking/live performances to help lead the crowd to desired outcome.<br /> <br /> Physically demanding artwork, like making sculptures would be a physical approach (from the physical effort of might to hew the stone, the finesse needed to get the details right with dexterity or just spending hours of exhausting effort on the project with stamina). Even painting can be physically demanding (more finesse and stamina than actual might though). More intellectual works, such as writing would probably fall under a Mental approach, while music and songs and similar social actions would of course be a Social approach.<br /> <br /> Acting and similar performance arts could see all 3 approaches... Physical, Mental and Social, depending on how they are done (Action movie stars are likely to be more physical, while Musicians are likely to be more Social oriented).<br /> <br /> Culture does seem to be the primary focus for artist/performers, with a few secondary skills to round out the types of performances they perform (Action Movie stars would likely need decent Athletics, while a Stage Magician would find Subterfuge useful). Persuasion and Empathy to connect with their audience and influence them in the desired ways would also be helpful. Leadership can also be helpful... especially for A-List actors that tend to take the lead... or Lead singers who help coordinate their band's acts (though this doesn't always mean that they are the one in charge... just in charge of the moment).<br /> <br /> The abstract approach may make skills quite broad for many purposes, but it does make things difficult to nail down what is most needed... especially when you want a specific use that doesn't seem covered by a specific skill or seems to fall into the area of multiple skills. I guess this is where specialties will come into play (with different specialties from different skills rounding out how one approaches a specific art form). Culture (Singing), Empathy (Reading Crowds) and Persuasion (Live Performances) would indicate the singer in a rock band to some degree... who can anticipate a crowd's reaction to different songs and decide what order to perform songs to make the event memorable for all. Throw in Athletics (Dance) for a choreographed routine... such as many Pop-Stars and performance bands... and you have the makings of an A-list performer. Switch to Culture (Entertainment) and Subterfuge (Slight of Hand or Escape Artist) and you have a Stage Magician who can wow a crowd in the manner of David Copperfield or Chris Angel.<br /> <br /> Does all this seem reasonable? Just want to be sure I have the right handle on how to work with the system we are being given (though it still needs a little polish in areas) before I decide if it is enough to work with or if it will need additional tweeking for my specific needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}